[
    {
        "role": "paragraph",
        "segment": "A strategy for finding a reusable component is to build an inventory and use a feature-based matrix to identify components whose features are needed by multiple projects, then target those features for reuse (and redesign them to be more reusable).",
        "citations": [
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "The Council created an inventory of components and formed a matrix with the features of all past  and  planned  projects. Then, each  feature  was  rated  in  terms  of  whether  it  had  been implemented and was still needed, had been implemented but was no longer needed, or had not been implemented but was still needed.Those features that were needed and were common to more than one project were targeted for reuse. In fact, some were redesigned to make them more reusable.",
                "img_id": null
            }
        ]
    },
    {
        "role": "paragraph",
        "segment": "Additionally, evaluate components against four practical guidelines: (1) Does the component perform the function or provide the data you need? (2) If minor modification is required, is it less modification than building the component from scratch? (3) Is the component well-documented, so you can understand it without verifying its implementation line by line? (4) Is there a complete record of the component's test and revision history, so you can be certain that it contains no faults?",
        "citations": [
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "guidelines for you. If you are a consumer for your current project, there are four key characteristics to check about the components you are about to reuse:\n\n1. Does the component perform the function or provide the data you need?\n2. If minor modification is required, is it less modification than building the component from scratch?\n3. Is the component well-documented, so you can understand it without having to verify its implementation line by line?\n4. Is there a complete record of the component's test and revision history, so you can be certain that it contains no faults?",
                "img_id": null
            }
        ]
    },
    {
        "role": "paragraph",
        "segment": "As a producer of reusable components, keep in mind that you should also ensure that your components are designed for reuse and that documentation and revision/test histories are maintained to facilitate future reuse.",
        "citations": [
            {
                "type": "source_text",
                "content": "On the other hand, if you are a producer of reusable components, you should keep in mind several things:",
                "img_id": null
            }
        ]
    }
]

